  <name>jellytoast</name>
  <summary>A desktop music player for Jellyfin and Navidrome servers</summary>

  <description>
    <p>
      jellytoast is a desktop music player for Jellyfin and Navidrome
      servers (and any Subsonic / OpenSubsonic server). Bit-perfect mpv
      playback, gapless audio, MPRIS2 system integration, system-tray
      controls, and a floating mini player.
    </p>
    <p>Features:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Browse albums, artists, songs, playlists, genres, and internet radio</li>
      <li>Native search across both providers with offline-aware filtering</li>
      <li>Bit-perfect mpv playback with optional server-side transcode tiers and ReplayGain (track / album)</li>
      <li>Casting: Chromecast, AirPlay 2, DLNA, and Sonos — each toggleable per-protocol</li>
      <li>Local cast relay for remote / Tailscale / self-signed servers (devices that can't reach the source)</li>
      <li>Explicit downloads with full offline playback (cascade by album / artist / playlist) and offline indicator</li>
      <li>Synced and plain lyrics, with a dedicated now-playing page</li>
      <li>Floating mini player with optional always-on-top on KDE Wayland</li>
      <li>MPRIS2 + system-tray integration; media-key support</li>
      <li>ListenBrainz scrobbling with offline queue</li>
      <li>Smart shuffle, smart playlists, sleep timer with fade-to-stop, tag editing (Jellyfin)</li>
      <li>Theming: built-in theme families (Catppuccin, Dracula, Gruvbox, Nord, and more), base16 import, a watched themes folder, pywal/wallust follow, system-accent follow, and a glass-opacity slider</li>
    </ul>
  </description>

